  "patch_scope": "Explicit CHOS CMake/bmalloc identity;owned-page discard;OS-brokered entropy with bounded retries and fail-closed errors;bounded native Console diagnostics. No local RNG,device fallback or full engine/security/conformance success inferred. Native mutex backoff uses the real scheduled YIELD service,not an unimplemented nanosleep API. Explicit WTF CHOS identity and private pthread selection; separate real native mutex/condition backend,not Unix signals/thread suspension. Native WTF clocks use checked realtime/monotonic services;unavailable clocks fail closed;continuous-time profile does not claim suspend/resume support. Native current-thread register layout and kernel-owned stack discovery;Unix signal-handler declarations excluded on CHOS. Foreign-thread suspend/GC/lifecycle remain unimplemented.",
